  Wall clock ≈ 14 h vs ~5.7 h serialized leaf work — the gap is Spring Batch metadata (141,752 BATCH_STEP_EXECUTION rows written to OLTP), flow transitions, transaction overhead, and
  the per-partition serial tail.

  The one-sentence diagnosis

  Cost is NOT data volume (605K claims is small — 59 claims/s).
  Cost IS iteration overhead: the enrichment flow re-launches 35,437 times
  (once per pharmacy) inside the partition, when it could run ONCE per
  partition over pharmacy_id IN (partition's ~1,750 pharmacies).

  The critical structural fact for any fix

    Phase 1 (enrichment)        Phase 2 (file writing)
    ─────────────────────       ──────────────────────
    ~100% of the cost           ~0% of the cost
    per-pharmacy loop is        per-pharmacy boundary is
    NOT load-bearing            LOAD-BEARING (headers/
    (just filters staging       trailers, per-pharmacy
    rows by pharmacy_id)        consolidation, ordering)
          │                             │
          └── safe to make bulk         └── must NOT be touched
              (pharmacy_id IN …)            (byte-for-byte identical)

  So the step-change (bulk per partition) lives entirely in Phase 1, which doesn't affect the output file's structure — Phase 2 keeps writing pharmacy-by-pharmacy exactly as today.
